# See https://docs.github.com/articles/about-codeowners for syntax.
# Order matters — later matches take precedence, so the most specific rules
# are listed after the tree-wide rule.
#
# NOTE: mirrors the same note in thyn-ai/algenta-sdk's CODEOWNERS. The
# thyn-ai org has exactly one member today (@0xamlab) and no teams. Every
# entry below is that one real account, not a placeholder — replace with a
# real team (@thyn-ai/codna-action-maintainers) as soon as a second
# maintainer joins. Until then, do NOT turn on the ruleset's "Require review
# from Code Owners" — GitHub blocks a PR author from approving their own PR,
# so a solo-owner CODEOWNERS with that setting on would make every PR
# unmergeable by the only person who can open one.

# Everything in this repository.
* @0xamlab

# action.yml is the product: its inputs, the mapping onto the codna command
# line, the install step and the token handling. A PR touching it gets
# flagged for deliberate review rather than being mergeable as an incidental
# part of a documentation change.
/action.yml @0xamlab

# The scripts are what CI executes on every pull request.
/scripts/ @0xamlab

# Workflow files are as security-sensitive as the code they run.
/.github/workflows/ @0xamlab
